<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dargo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Dargo expedition · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasian-war">Caucasian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dargo was a Russian expedition in 1845 under Prince Mikhail Vorontsov against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam-shamil">Imam Shamil</a>'s capital at Dargo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechnya">Chechnya</a>. The Russians took and burned the village, but on their retreat through the forests they suffered heavy losses to Shamil's fighters. The disaster led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> to adopt a slower strategy of clearing forests and building forts.</p></div>
